From 2222222222222222222222222222222222222222 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] lib: make INTERVAL_TREE user-selectable

INTERVAL_TREE is a promptless select-only symbol, enabled only when a driver
that uses it (i915, amdgpu, vfio, ...) selects it. The out-of-tree kgsl-dlkm
(proprietary Adreno UMD) links the exported interval_tree_* symbols, but on a
headless GPU config nothing selects INTERVAL_TREE, so kgsl-dlkm fails modpost
with "interval_tree_insert/remove/iter_first/iter_next undefined".

Give the symbol a prompt so a config fragment can enable it independently, which
also exports its symbols. This matches the linux-qcom reference kernel that
builds with CONFIG_INTERVAL_TREE=y.

Signed-off-by: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [gives a promptless symbol a prompt for the out-of-tree kgsl-dlkm]
---
 lib/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/Kconfig b/lib/Kconfig
--- a/lib/Kconfig
+++ b/lib/Kconfig
@@ -329,7 +329,7 @@
 	bool

 config INTERVAL_TREE
-	bool
+	bool "Interval tree"
 	help
 	  Simple, embeddable, interval-tree. Can find the start of an
 	  overlapping range in log(n) time and then iterate over all
